ve (12 consecutive quarters, no single-quarter exception).\",\"by_when\":\"Mar 31, 2032\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"My recession add-on arithmetic (+0.50 ordinary, +0.42 deep-tail, giving a 5.72% window mean) is too pessimistic and the demographic U-lowering term is larger than the -0.3 pp I assigned. CQ1 rises from 16 to ~26 (conjunct 1 to ~58%, conjunct 2 unchanged at 22% since the fiscal-monopsony obstacle is untouched by labour tightness); CQ3 P50 rises ~0.2 pp on hours; CQ6-A rises ~4 pp. Note this signpost moves ONLY the first conjunct - it is diagnostic of my labour-market arithmetic, not of my wage arithmetic.\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Reported OECD-38 + China strict operational data-centre electricity consumption for calendar year 2032 comes in at >= 900 TWh (against ~365 TWh in 2024), on a strict-operational basis comparable to the AI-Q3 definition.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2033 (reporting lag allowed)\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"My cost-of-capital brake on AI capex is not binding, the realized AI-Q3 quantity belongs near its locked P50 of 998 rather than the P10-P25 range of 600-800 that I argued for, and the adapter's model-versus-lock datacenter disagreement resolves in the model's favour rather than mine. CQ3 P50 rises ~0.25 pp (capital deepening and TFP both); CQ6-A rises ~5 pp; CQ4 P50 rises ~20 bps, since the AI/grid capex claim on loanable funds that I haircut from +25 to +10 bps would be restored; CQ5 falls ~3 pp (a realized build means less impairment, so a smaller 2a).\"} | {\"signpost\":\"Real median hourly compensation in ISIC Q (health and social work) for the OECD-38 aggregate exceeds its 2025 level by >= 8% deflated by local CPI, on a published harmonized basis.\",\"by_when\":\"Dec 31, 2033\",\"if_observed_implies\":\"My fiscal-monopsony claim - that care's shadow price rises but is not paid, and that the adjustment is volume rationing - has failed, and public employers have in fact outbid debt service. CQ1 rises from 16 to ~30 (conjunct 2 roughly doubles to ~42%); plank (a) rises ~10 to ~17 (the pay side of the transition works even if the matching side does not); CQ6-B rises ~5 pp at C's and D's expense (broad-based physical-sector wage gains with contained inflation is the barbell's benign leg); CQ2's OECD core conjunct rises ~4 pp, since an 8% real care-wage award at Q's ~10-11% GVA share is itself a ~0.3-0.4 pp cost-push impulse.\"}","updateBasis":{"kind":"launch","note":"run2 wave 1 fermi seat, effort 'rstar'."}}